HashMap-
    - It is class in java that stores data in key value pairs.
    

When we use- 
        -when we need fast data access. (it is mostly used in backend for APIs.)
        -in HashMap we can easy lookup using keys.
        -No need to look like ArrayList.


HashSet-
        -it is Collection that stores only unique values.
        -in HashSet order is not maintained.
        -it is good at performance.
        -it is used when we need unique values and no need to maintain the order and want best performance.


        ########## Note-
        Hashing is technique to convert data into a fixed number. so that we can store and retrive data fast.
        here fixed number is Hashcode.